   "about": "sdkconfig switches the EMAC to generate the RMII clock out on GPIO17, but the board feeds an external oscillator to GPIO0 and the LAN8720, and GPIO17 is the WROVER's PSRAM clock, so PSRAM breaks and the MAC runs on a clock unrelated to the PHY's.",
   "blind": "ESP-IDF Programming Guide, Ethernet, 'RMII clock' (CONFIG_ETH_RMII_CLK_INPUT on GPIO0 vs CONFIG_ETH_RMII_CLK_OUTPUT on GPIO0/16/17) and note that GPIO16/17 are taken by PSRAM on WROVER modules; ESP32-WROVER-E datasheet, pin description (GPIO16/17 connected to PSRAM)",
   "edits": [
